WEBVTT

1
00:00:16.044 --> 00:00:22.851
Cosette could not help casting one last look toward the beautiful doll displayed in the toy-shop stall.

2
00:00:22.852 --> 00:00:25.947
Then she knocked on the door of the inn.

3
00:00:25.948 --> 00:00:31.409
"Here you are at last!" said Madame Thenardier as she threw open the door.

4
00:00:31.410 --> 00:00:37.185
"You certainly took your time getting that water. What were you doing—playing?"

5
00:00:37.186 --> 00:00:43.510
"Madame," said Cosette, trembling, "here's a gentleman who needs a room."

6
00:00:43.511 --> 00:00:48.230
Madame Thenardier quickly replaced her fierce scowl with a friendly demeanor.

7
00:00:48.231 --> 00:00:51.185
"Come in, monsieur. Welcome!"

8
00:00:51.186 --> 00:00:59.090
As Jean Valjean stepped inside, she caught sight of his long, threadbare yellow coat and his tattered hat.

9
00:00:59.091 --> 00:01:06.765
His luggage consisted of a walking stick and a mysterious bundle. She glanced at her husband and wrinkled her nose.

10
00:01:06.766 --> 00:01:13.233
The innkeeper, who was sitting with some of the inn's guests, nodded in response.

11
00:01:13.234 --> 00:01:20.828
"Oh, I'm sorry, my good man," said Madame Thenardier, "but we have no rooms available."

12
00:01:20.829 --> 00:01:27.987
"Put me wherever you have space—in the garret, in the stable. I'll be happy to pay as if I had a regular room."

13
00:01:27.988 --> 00:01:31.891
"That'll be forty sous, paid in advance."

14
00:01:31.892 --> 00:01:38.971
"Forty sous?" whispered one of the guests to Monsieur Thenardier. "I thought a room was only twenty sous."

15
00:01:38.972 --> 00:01:48.042
"It's forty sous for him," replied the innkeeper. "We try to discourage guests like him. They ruin the inn's reputation."

16
00:01:48.043 --> 00:01:53.934
Meanwhile Valjean handed the cash to Madame Thenardier and took a seat at another table.

17
00:01:53.935 --> 00:01:59.781
Cosette quickly brought him something to drink and then took water to the guest's horse.

18
00:01:59.782 --> 00:02:08.543
When Cosette returned and resumed her place under the kitchen table with her knitting, Valjean couldn't take his eyes off her.

19
00:02:08.544 --> 00:02:15.694
This plain, thin little girl had dark circles under her eyes, which were dull from constant weeping.

20
00:02:15.695 --> 00:02:23.519
Her hands and bare legs were red and rough. Everything she wore was made of cotton and full of holes.

21
00:02:23.520 --> 00:02:28.840
She was shivering, so she drew up her knees and hugged them to her chest while she knit.

22
00:02:28.841 --> 00:02:34.432
Cosette was still wet from getting the water but didn't dare to warm herself by the fire.

23
00:02:34.433 --> 00:02:41.511
Fear made her take up the smallest possible space and prevented her from breathing more than necessary.

24
00:02:41.512 --> 00:02:47.003
Suddenly Madame Thenardier shouted, "Oh! Where is that bread?"

25
00:02:47.004 --> 00:02:53.066
Cosette, as she always did whenever Madame Thenardier raised her voice, sprang from under the table.

26
00:02:53.067 --> 00:02:59.918
The child had completely forgotten the bread, so she did the only thing she could think of. She lied.

27
00:02:59.919 --> 00:03:02.833
"Madame, the bakery was closed."

28
00:03:02.834 --> 00:03:05.654
"You should have knocked!"

29
00:03:05.655 --> 00:03:07.764
"I did, but no one answered."

30
00:03:07.765 --> 00:03:15.900
"I'll find out tomorrow if that's true, and if you're lying, you'll be in trouble. Give me the 15-sous coin."

31
00:03:15.901 --> 00:03:21.805
Cosette plunged her hand into her apron pocket and turned white. The coin was gone.

32
00:03:21.806 --> 00:03:28.821
She turned the pocket inside out, but there was still nothing. The poor girl was too frightened to utter a word.

33
00:03:28.822 --> 00:03:34.556
"Have you lost it or did you try to steal it from me?" screamed Madame Thenardier.

34
00:03:34.557 --> 00:03:38.043
She reached for a whip hanging near the fireplace.

35
00:03:38.044 --> 00:03:41.044
"Forgive me, madame!" cried Cosette.

36
00:03:41.045 --> 00:03:47.376
Watching this scene unfold, Valjean deftly removed a coin from his own waistcoat pocket.

37
00:03:47.377 --> 00:03:54.694
"I beg your pardon, madame," said Valjean, "but I just saw something fall out of the little girl's pocket and roll away."

38
00:03:54.695 --> 00:03:59.606
At the same time, he stooped down and appeared to search the floor.

39
00:03:59.607 --> 00:04:05.360
"Aha, here it is!" He handed Madame Thenardier a silver coin.

40
00:04:05.361 --> 00:04:07.908
"Yes, that's it."

41
00:04:07.909 --> 00:04:18.177
She put the coin in her own apron pocket and contented herself with giving Cosette a ferocious look and saying, "Don't ever let that happen again."

42
00:04:18.178 --> 00:04:26.344
Valjean's coin was actually a twenty-sous piece. That made up for the lack of bread as far as Madame Thenardier was concerned.

43
00:04:26.345 --> 00:04:30.431
A door now opened and Eponine and Azelma came in.

44
00:04:30.432 --> 00:04:35.177
They were so lively, neat, and plump that it was a pleasure to look at them.

45
00:04:35.178 --> 00:04:42.740
Madame Thenardier took them on her lap, one at a time, smoothing their hair and retying their hair ribbons.

46
00:04:42.741 --> 00:04:46.069
"What good girls they are!" she said.

47
00:04:46.070 --> 00:04:49.319
They went and sat by the fire and played with a doll.

48
00:04:49.320 --> 00:04:56.962
From time to time, Cosette raised her eyes from her knitting and looked sadly at them as they played.

49
00:04:56.963 --> 00:05:00.791
Eponine and Azelma paid no attention to Cosette.

50
00:05:00.792 --> 00:05:07.724
Their doll was old and faded, but it still seemed wonderful to Cosette, who had never had a doll.

51
00:05:07.725 --> 00:05:13.716
All of a sudden Madame Thenardier noticed that Cosette was watching the girls instead of knitting.

52
00:05:13.717 --> 00:05:19.342
"Is that how you work?" she cried. "I'll make you work with the whip, I will."

53
00:05:19.343 --> 00:05:22.121
"Oh, let her play," said Valjean.

54
00:05:22.122 --> 00:05:27.684
Now if a wealthy guest had made this request, Madame Thenardier might have agreed.

55
00:05:27.686 --> 00:05:31.121
But to hear such a thing from a pauper like this man!

56
00:05:31.122 --> 00:05:39.367
"She has to work in order to eat," snapped Madame Thenardier. "I don't support her so she can do nothing."

57
00:05:39.368 --> 00:05:40.860
"What's she making?"

58
00:05:40.861 --> 00:05:46.605
"Stockings for my girls, who have none to speak of and will soon be going barefoot."

59
00:05:46.606 --> 00:05:52.438
Valjean looked at Cosette's chapped red feet. "When will she be finished with a pair of stockings?"

60
00:05:52.439 --> 00:05:56.343
"It'll take her at least three or four days, the lazy thing."

61
00:05:56.344 --> 00:06:04.335
"If I pay you five francs, will you let her play?" asked Valjean. His offer was almost five times what the stockings were worth.

62
00:06:04.336 --> 00:06:09.586
Monsieur Thenardier decided to join the conversation now that Valjean was spending money.

63
00:06:09.587 --> 00:06:13.994
"If you want to pay that much for a pair of stockings, we can't refuse you."

64
00:06:13.995 --> 00:06:20.661
Valjean turned to Cosette and said, "Now your work belongs to me, and I say you should play."

65
00:06:20.662 --> 00:06:26.060
"Is it true, madame?" asked Cosette. "Can I really play?"

66
00:06:26.061 --> 00:06:31.137
"Play!" said Madame Thenardier in a terrible voice.

67
00:06:31.138 --> 00:06:39.915
Cosette did not move from her spot under the table. She reached behind her and took out a little toy sword and a few old rags.

68
00:06:39.916 --> 00:06:44.893
She pretended that the sword was a doll and the rags were its clothes.

69
00:06:44.894 --> 00:06:49.208
Meanwhile Eponine and Azelma had abandoned their doll.

70
00:06:49.209 --> 00:06:54.034
They had caught the cat and were busy trying to dress it in doll clothes.

71
00:06:54.035 --> 00:06:59.780
"This little girl is not your own child?" Valjean asked Madame Thenardier.

72
00:06:59.781 --> 00:07:07.304
"No, her mother left her with us. We do all we can for her, but we aren't rich.

73
00:07:07.305 --> 00:07:12.272
We haven't heard from her mother for months, so we suspect she's dead."

74
00:07:12.273 --> 00:07:18.046
Cosette overheard this conversation and said to herself, "My mother is dead!"

75
00:07:18.047 --> 00:07:22.772
But as hard as she tried, she could not remember anything about her mother.

76
00:07:22.773 --> 00:07:27.685
She darted out and brought the girls' doll back under the table.

77
00:07:27.686 --> 00:07:32.431
There she played with it for some time until Azelma noticed what was happening.

78
00:07:32.432 --> 00:07:35.987
"Mother!" she cried. "Look there!"

79
00:07:35.988 --> 00:07:41.431
"Cosette!" shouted Madame Thenardier. "Stop playing with that doll!"

80
00:07:41.432 --> 00:07:48.082
Sobbing, Cosette came out from under the table and laid the doll at Madame Thenardier's feet.

81
00:07:48.083 --> 00:07:54.994
"Why is it a problem that Cosette is playing with the doll?" asked Valjean. "The girls weren't using it."

82
00:07:54.995 --> 00:08:01.065
"That beggar dared to touch my children's doll with her horrid, dirty hands."

83
00:08:01.066 --> 00:08:05.777
Valjean walked straight to the door, opened it, and went outside.

84
00:08:05.778 --> 00:08:11.161
In a few minutes he returned with the beautiful doll from the Christmas stall.

85
00:08:11.162 --> 00:08:18.551
"Here, Cosette," he said, tenderly laying the doll in her arms. "This is for you."
